---
/**
 * The Otter Homecare mascot, inline so CSS can move it.
 *
 * The file at public/assets/otter-mascot.svg used to reference 17 style classes
 * and define none of them, so it rendered as a solid black silhouette — which is
 * why every mascot on the site was a PNG. Both are repaired now; the fills here
 * were sampled from otter-mascot.png rather than guessed.
 *
 * Inline rather than <img> because an image cannot be animated from outside.
 * Fills are scoped under #otterMascot so the generic .st* names cannot leak into
 * the page. Motion lives in code-overrides.css and hooks the site's own .reveal/.in
 * observer, so it needs no JavaScript of its own.
 */
---
